data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_b2e69fb2336d4fe6b321b086","messageId":"bc0b069d-5c7c-4710-ad84-855b983df96f","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"artifactId\":\"ctx-6b3588e4a11aa63f2606201507c097352f076cea325b422a26add181b1cbc901\",\"historical\":true,\"grantsFreshness\":false,\"originalTool\":\"read_file\",\"path\":[\"result\",\"content\"],\"kind\":\"string\",\"keys\":[],\"keyCount\":0,\"content\":\"_SERVICE`; `useAgentUITheme` needs `AGENT_UI_THEME_SERVICE`, each in `inject` or `optionalInject` as appropriate. Theme CSS tokens alone do not need the theme hook.\\n103: 7. Add styles using the generated project's existing styling approach; do not introduce a UI library or dependency without project support.\\n104:    Import a Plugin stylesheet once. For ordinary action buttons, use the\\n105:    project's inspected public Button facade when one exists.\\n106: 8. Default-export the definition so the target-owned generator can include it in the static Registry. Do not spread a template catalog into the production registry.\\n107: 9. Submit `pluginId` and all currently known new Plugin files together in one `create_ui_plugin` call, using `relativePath` values inside that Plugin directory. It requires `manifest.json`, `definition.ts`, and `index.tsx`, is create-only, and transactionally rolls back the whole call on failure. Never use it to replace an existing Plugin directory or file.\\n108: 10. Run `validate_creator_changes`. Fix returned diagnostics with `read_file` plus `edit_file`, then validate the new revision again.\\n109: 11. Add exactly one AppUIPluginNode through `mutate_app_ui_model`. When an\\n110:     eligible relative `defaultPlacement` declares the intended side panel,\\n111:     use `insert_plugin_default` so the Host places it beside the anchor in the\\n112:     public Layout and preserves the Platform drawer track. Do not insert it into\\n113:     the conversation's existing Slot or nest a Row inside its Panel. Use a\\n114:     low-level Layout operation only for a different authorized location after\\n115:     checking its root track and responsive contract. An Application Gate goes\\n116:     at application scope. The transaction updates the generated Registry.\\n117: 12. Because composition changes the Activity revision, run `validate_creator_changes` again for the final revision.\\n118: 13. In `static_and_runtime` mode, call `inspect_runtime_errors`. Fresh current-hash evidence with zero current errors is required before claiming Runtime success. In `static_only` mode, stop after current-revision static validation and do not claim Runtime success.\\n119: \\n120: \\n121: ## Contract boundaries\\n122: \\n123: ### Application Gate contract\\n124: \\n125: Use `manifest.application.gate` when entry to the Workspace must be denied until a condition is ready. Do not model this requirement as a modal, overlay, root/main Slot contribution, dedicated Login Slot, or high-z-index element, and do not change the Layout Tree merely to host it.\\n126: \\n127: - The Gate manifest names one observable Service and may assign a numeric priority. Do not also add an `app-gate` capability; `application.gate` is the single source of truth and is distinct from `headless`.\\n128: - The definition declares the Gate Service in `provides`, and `setup()` synchronously provides it with an initial `checking`, `blocked`, `ready`, or `error` snapshot. Async session recovery begins only after the observable Service is available.\\n129: - A Gate plugin node is `enabled: true` in `applicationPlugins`. A Gate manifest must not declare child Slots.\\n130: - Gate hard dependencies use `inject`. Every Provider in that dependency closure must be an application-scoped `headless` Plugin or another Application Gate. `optionalInject` never expands the startup dependency closure.\\n131: - The Gate component may read its own provided Gate Service with `usePluginService()`. This self-read permission applies to Components only; `setup({ services }).get()` still reads only `inject` and `optionalInject` dependencies.\\n132: - Multiple Gates all must become `ready`. Priority selects which non-ready Gate surface is currently displayed; it does not weaken the all-ready rule.\\n133: - Gate state is frontend Application lifecycle state. Never add AG-UI custom events or modify Agent protocol semantics to control it.\\n134: \\n135: For requests such as “不登录不能进入应用”, “打开应用必须先登录”, “没有 License 不能使用”, “必须先选择组织”, or “初始化完成前不能进入工作台”, inspect existing Gate/Auth assets and Services first, then create or reuse an Application Gate without introducing a Login Slot or Layout overlay.\\n136: \\n137: ### Child Slot contract\\n138: \\n139: When adding, removing, or renaming a child `renderSlot(...)` outlet in a container Plugin, update `manifest.json` `slots.children` in the same task. Each local Slot name maps to a required `description`, `cardinality: \\\"one\\\" | \\\"many\\\"`, and optional `optional` flag. Names must be static string literals; do not create dynamic `renderSlot(slot)` outlets or global Runtime slot ids. Host verification treats the Plugin source and manifest child Slot sets as an exact contract.\\n140: \\n141: For an npm-backed Plugin, the project application may add a new semantic outlet\\n142: without source takeover. Preserve every installed canonical child Slot unchanged,\\n143: declare the additional Slot in the local manifest, expose that combined manifest\\n144: from the local definition, and render the new outlet explicitly in the application.\\n145: Keep forwarding the original props and Slots into the npm component. The Host\\n146: combines only the additional local Slots with the installed canonical contract;\\n147: the npm component does not implicitly render project-added outlets.\\n148: \\n149: For a runtime entity renderer, declare `mode: \\\"renderer\\\"`, `cardinality: \\\"one\\\"`, and `accepts.anyOfCapabilities`, then call `renderScopedSlot(\\\"localName\\\", scope)`. Renderer Slots have no implicit presentation fallback. A fallback must be explicitly supplied by the owning parent; otherwise an empty, disabled, unavailable, inactive, or capability-mismatched occupant renders nothing. Omitted `mode` means ordinary content. The renderer Plugin reads `usePluginRenderScope()` and checks its `kind`; a Plugin that requires scope declares `requiresRenderScope: true` and returns `null` without the expected scope. Prefer changing the renderer Plugin instance in AppUIModel when changing Reasoning, Tool Group, or Tool Fallback presentation. Keep Agent UI grouping, part order, named Tool UI selection, and message lifecycle in the canonical Thread.\\n150: \\n151: - Read Agent data through the installed Runtime public APIs and the project's existing domain/Service Hooks. Inspect their actual exports and signatures; initialized projects do not contain a local `/runtime/context` module. Keep the existing Provider and canonical Conversation Runtime.\\n152: - Read the current instance scope through `usePluginInstance`, `usePluginActions`, and `usePluginEvents`. Never recreate a combined context prop or pass Runtime snapshot fields through component props.\\n153: - Before a Plugin consumes a backend Application Event, inspect the existing `Agent.appEventSchemas` binding and `/agent-contract/agent-events.ts` when present, reuse or add the application-owned payload schema, then declare the same exact name in `manifest.data.events`. Preserve an explicitly supplied Custom Event name exactly; lowercase dot-separated naming is recommended only when the application has not already chosen a name. A manifest declaration consumes an application-owned contract; it does not register one.\\n154: - Prefer the project-local `subscribeAppEvent` helper so the registered payload type is inferred; `usePluginEvents().subscribe` and `setup({ events })` remain the underlying scoped APIs. Never import AG-UI protocol event types into Plugin code, invent a schema inside a Plugin, emit an Application Event from the frontend, or use this channel for persistent state, standard lifecycle, Activity, interrupts, Frontend Tools, or local Plugin communication. If the backend payload contract is unknown, ask for it instead of inventing fields.\\n155: - Use `usePluginActions()` for instance-scoped Agent commands and the installed Runtime's public Host API for application-owned commands. Keep transient UI state out of AppUIModel; use private component state within one Plugin and Services across Plugins. Never create a separate Agent Runtime inside a\",\"offset\":8000,\"nextOffset\":16000,\"totalCharacters\":26123}}","role":"tool"}

