data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_32e5584398a64d4c85d7999f","messageId":"d398bb37-c0a2-4927-adfb-821457a089dd","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"appUIModelHash\":\"ec814f21d2857a86f24a3cd35ae3cbc8d079f4b634bd7553dc7738d8ba4c5d7c\",\"asset\":{\"ownership\":\"project_source\",\"pluginId\":\"test-notice\",\"name\":\"Test Notice\",\"description\":\"Displays a static bilingual notice at the top of the chat area using React native elements and theme tokens.\",\"directory\":\"test-notice\",\"manifestPath\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/manifest.json\",\"definitionPath\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/definition.ts\",\"capabilities\":[\"test-notice\"],\"authoring\":{\"intents\":[\"show a test notice at the chat top\",\"显示测试提示\",\"在聊天区域顶部显示提示\"],\"visualRole\":\"chat area top notice\",\"defaultPlacement\":{\"type\":\"relative\",\"relation\":\"above\",\"anchorPluginId\":\"conversation-surface\"},\"recommendedSize\":{\"height\":\"40px\"}},\"childSlots\":{},\"dataMessageUINames\":[],\"selected\":true},\"sharedTypes\":{\"status\":\"available\",\"queryResolution\":{\"status\":\"complete\",\"requested\":3,\"resolved\":3,\"unresolved\":0},\"statusMeaning\":\"available means the installed declaration module was inspected; queryResolution and each symbol status describe whether the requested contracts resolved.\",\"packageVersion\":\"0.0.1\",\"module\":\"@za38.03/agent-ui-plugins\",\"symbols\":[{\"name\":\"useAgentUILocale\",\"status\":\"available\",\"type\":\"{ (): AgentUILocaleMessages; <N extends keyof AgentUILocaleMessages>(namespace: N): AgentUILocaleMessages[N]; }\",\"truncated\":false,\"memberNames\":[],\"memberNamesTruncated\":false,\"members\":[],\"membersTruncated\":false,\"returns\":[{\"type\":\"AgentUILocaleMessages\",\"truncated\":false},{\"type\":\"AgentUILocaleMessages[N]\",\"truncated\":false}],\"signaturesTruncated\":false},{\"name\":\"AgentUILocaleMessages\",\"status\":\"available\",\"type\":\"AgentUILocaleMessages\",\"truncated\":false,\"memberNames\":[\"layout\",\"toolResult\",\"humanQuestion\",\"copyAction\",\"theme\",\"conversationTriggers\",\"agentIdentity\",\"conversationQuote\",\"transientMessages\",\"auth\",\"thinkingIndicator\",\"toolTimeline\",\"common\",\"composer\",\"conversationFeedback\",\"starterSuggestions\",\"conversation\",\"threadList\",\"serviceAdapters\",\"attachments\",\"images\",\"quote\",\"tasks\",\"triggers\",\"accessibility\",\"searchTools\",\"search\",\"examples\",\"runtime\",\"themeShowcase\",\"media\",\"files\",\"questionOptions\",\"toolPresentation\",\"composerTriggerDemo\",\"frontendTools\"],\"memberNamesTruncated\":false,\"members\":[{\"name\":\"layout\",\"type\":\"{ open: string; close: string; collapse: string; restore: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"toolResult\",\"type\":\"{ resolving: string; unavailable: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"humanQuestion\",\"type\":\"{ back: string; next: string; submit: string; submitting: string; answered: string; noneSelected: string; unavailable: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"copyAction\",\"type\":\"{ failed: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"theme\",\"type\":\"{ settings: string; light: string; dark: string; violet: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"conversationTriggers\",\"type\":\"{ suggestions: string; back: string; empty: string; loading: string; searchFailed: string; retry: string; commandFailed: string; invalidItem: string; newConversation: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"agentIdentity\",\"type\":\"{ name: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"conversationQuote\",\"type\":\"{ quote: string; dismiss: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"transientMessages\",\"type\":\"{ systemMessage: string; userMessage: string; assistantMessage: string; errorMessage: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"auth\",\"type\":\"{ title: string; checking: string; account: string; password: string; signIn: string; signOut: string; working: string; signInFailed: string; signOutFailed: string; notSignedIn: string; accountMenu: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"thinkingIndicator\",\"type\":\"{ thinking: string; working: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"toolTimeline\",\"type\":\"{ summaryWithOneFile: string; summaryWithFiles: string; pendingSummary: string; summary: string; active: string; read: string; command: string; search: string; edit: string; tool: string; complete: string; ... 5 more ...; unknown: string; }\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"common\",\"type\":\"{ close: string; copy: string; refresh: string; edit: string; cancel: string; update: string; previous: string; next: string; show: string; more: string; back: string; retry: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"composer\",\"type\":\"{ awaitingReply: string; placeholder: string; input: string; addAttachment: string; voiceInput: string; startVoice: string; stopDictation: string; stopVoice: string; send: string; queueSend: string; stop: string; cancelSend: string; queued:\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"conversationFeedback\",\"type\":\"{ helpful: string; notHelpful: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"starterSuggestions\",\"type\":\"{ architectureTitle: string; architectureLabel: string; architecturePrompt: string; debugTitle: string; debugLabel: string; debugPrompt: string; nextTitle: string; nextLabel: string; nextPrompt: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"conversation\",\"type\":\"{ generationStopped: string; editInput: string; loading: string; scrollToBottom: string; welcome: string; working: string; moreActions: string; exportMarkdown: string; reasoning: string; reasoningDuration: string; editCancel: string; editUp\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"threadList\",\"type\":\"{ historyTitle: string; retry: string; newChat: string; moreOptions: string; running: string; rename: string; archive: string; unarchive: string; archived: string; delete: string; loading: string; ... 8 more ...; earlier: string; }\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"serviceAdapters\",\"type\":\"{ requestFailed: string; invalidResponse: string; invalidUploadUrl: string; invalidConfig: string; fileTypeRejected: string; fileTooLarge: string; dictationFailed: string; recordingUnavailable: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"attachments\",\"type\":\"{ previewNamed: string; removeNamed: string; tileNamed: string; named: string; namedUploading: string; namedFailed: string; preview: string; previewFailed: string; imagePreview: string; uploadFailed: string; ... 11 more ...; demoReadFailed:\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"images\",\"type\":\"{ content: string; newTab: string; preview: string; zoom: string; zoomed: string; closeZoom: string; generating: string; generationFailed: string; regenerate: string; download: string; copy: string; blocked: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"quote\",\"type\":\"{ quote: string; dismiss: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"tasks\",\"type\":\"{ title: string; running: string; waiting: string; failed: string; done: string; working: string; waitingState: string; failedState: string; childFailed: string; doneState: string; cancelledState: string; ... 7 more ...; groupFailed: string\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"triggers\",\"type\":\"{ noItems: string; noResults: string; suggestions: string; back: string; empty: string; loading: string; searchFailed: string; retry: string; commandFailed: string; invalidItem: string; items: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"accessibility\",\"type\":\"{ sidebar: string; sidebarDescription: string; toggleSidebar: string; language: string; chineseName: string; englishName: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"searchTools\",\"type\":\"{ searching: string; sources: string; retrieving: string; passages: string; relevance: string; score: string; contextKnowledgeBase: string; contextLongTermMemory: string; contextCount: string; contextQuery: string; contextEmpty: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"search\",\"type\":\"{ searching: string; readSources: string; searchFiles: string; searchedFiles: string; noFiles: string; oneFile: string; manyFiles: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"examples\",\"type\":\"{ hostAnalyzeButton: string; hostAnalyzePrompt: string; hostCloseAssistant: string; hostOpenAssistant: string; hostSendFailed: string; presentationEditor: string; presentationDocument: string; ... 85 more ...; embeddedAssistant: string; }\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"runtime\",\"type\":\"{ pluginRenderFailed: string; assistant: string; openAssistant: string; closeAssistant: string; startupFailed: string; unknownGateError: string; gateCannotRender: string; pluginNotifications: string; ... 5 more ...; missingInstance: string;\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"themeShowcase\",\"type\":\"{ title: string; theme: string; light: string; dark: string; violet: string; welcome: string; welcomeText: string; user: string; assistant: string; composer: string; send: string; stop: string; primary: string; ... 26 more ...; result: stri\",\"truncated\":true},{\"name\":\"media\",\"type\":\"{ audio: string; video: string; play: string; pause: string; seek: string; position: string; audioError: string; }\",\"truncated\":false},{\"name\":\"files\",\"type\":\"{ unnamed: string; download: string; }\",\"truncated\":false}],\"membersTruncated\":true,\"returns\":[],\"signaturesTruncated\":false},{\"name\":\"AgentUILocaleCode\",\"status\":\"available\",\"type\":\"AgentUILocaleCode\",\"truncated\":false,\"memberNames\":[],\"memberNamesTruncated\":false,\"union\":{\"commonMembersOnly\":true,\"variants\":[{\"query\":\"AgentUILocaleCode.$variant0\",\"queryAvailable\":true,\"type\":\"\\\"en-US\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"discriminants\":[],\"members\":[],\"membersTruncated\":false},{\"query\":\"AgentUILocaleCode.$variant1\",\"queryAvailable\":true,\"type\":\"\\\"zh-CN\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"discriminants\":[],\"members\":[],\"membersTruncated\":false}],\"variantsTruncated\":false,\"interpretation\":\"Top-level members are shared by all union branches. A member absent there may exist in a variant. Query the returned exact variant path to inspect its members and invocation parameters.\"},\"members\":[],\"membersTruncated\":false,\"returns\":[],\"signaturesTruncated\":false}],\"interpretation\":\"Installed public types and package-owned presentation contracts, not mutation authority. Queries: export.member; $parameter0 through $parameter9 for invocation props; $return for callable return; $element for array/index values; returned $variant0 through $variant7 paths for union branches. Types establish signatures, not runtime semantics; missing behavior facts must remain unverified. Unresolved queries and omitted details are explicit. Each presentation contract is returned once per root export in this response.\"},\"selected\":true,\"instances\":[{\"id\":\"p23\",\"pluginId\":\"test-notice\",\"enabled\":true,\"target\":{\"type\":\"layout_slot\",\"slotRef\":\"l8\"},\"index\":0,\"effectiveEnabled\":true,\"runtimeInstanceId\":\"p23\"}],\"manifest\":{\"id\":\"test-notice\",\"name\":\"Test Notice\",\"description\":\"Displays a static bilingual notice at the top of the chat area using React native elements and theme tokens.\",\"version\":\"0.0.1\",\"capabilities\":[\"test-notice\"],\"authoring\":{\"intents\":[\"show a test notice at the chat top\",\"显示测试提示\",\"在聊天区域顶部显示提示\"],\"visualRole\":\"chat area top notice\",\"recommendedSize\":{\"height\":\"40px\"},\"defaultPlacement\":{\"type\":\"relative\",\"relation\":\"above\",\"anchorPluginId\":\"conversation-surface\"}}},\"definitionSource\":{\"content\":\"import type { UIPluginDefinition, UIPluginManifest } from \\\"@za38.03/agent-ui-plugins\\\";\\nimport manifestJson from \\\"./manifest.json\\\";\\nimport { TestNoticePlugin } from \\\"./index\\\";\\n\\nconst definition: UIPluginDefinition = {\\n  manifest: manifestJson as UIPluginManifest,\\n  provides: [],\\n  inject: [],\\n  optionalInject: [\\\"agent-ui.locale\\\"],\\n  Component: TestNoticePlugin,\\n};\\n\\nexport default definition;\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"characters\":394},\"services\":{\"provides\":[],\"required\":[],\"optional\":[\"agent-ui.locale\"]},\"files\":[{\"path\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/definition.ts\",\"kind\":\"file\",\"bytes\":394},{\"path\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/index.tsx\",\"kind\":\"file\",\"bytes\":522},{\"path\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/manifest.json\",\"kind\":\"file\",\"bytes\":634},{\"path\":\"src/agent-ui/plugins/test-notice/styles.css\",\"kind\":\"file\",\"bytes\":295}],\"filesTruncated\":false}}","role":"tool"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_START","toolCallId":"call_0bdc1fb6bf704da1b8cca450","toolCallName":"read_creator_context"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"call_0bdc1fb6bf704da1b8cca450","delta":"{\"artifactId\":\"ctx-6b3588e4a11aa63f2606201507c097352f076cea325b422a26add181b1cbc901\",\"limit\":8000,\"offset\":16000,\"path\":[\"result\",\"content\"]}"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_END","toolCallId":"call_0bdc1fb6bf704da1b8cca450"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_0bdc1fb6bf704da1b8cca450","messageId":"7872cc26-58db-40ff-b4f6-ad408bca7505","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"artifactId\":\"ctx-6b3588e4a11aa63f2606201507c097352f076cea325b422a26add181b1cbc901\",\"historical\":true,\"grantsFreshness\":false,\"originalTool\":\"read_file\",\"path\":[\"result\",\"content\"],\"kind\":\"string\",\"keys\":[],\"keyCount\":0,\"content\":\" Plugin.\\n156: - Keep Plugin dependencies in the generated project and follow its current UI stack and versions.\\n157: - Service contracts are stable project-owned capability seams, not concrete\\n158:   Provider Plugins or Runtime Core actions:\\n159:   - `provides` means this Plugin owns and declares one or more capabilities for the current activation lifecycle.\\n160:   - `inject` means this Plugin requires a hard capability dependency before activation.\\n161:   - `optionalInject` means this Plugin can use an enhancement but remains complete and active without it.\\n162:   - `usePluginService()` is runtime capability lookup for component access; `setup({ services })` remains the non-React activation API.\\n163: - Provider rules are strict: if `setup` calls `services.provide`, the Plugin **must** declare the same Service Name in `UIPluginDefinition.provides`.\\n164: - For a hard capability dependency, import its stable Service seam from `/services/*` and declare `inject` on `UIPluginDefinition`; do not import concrete Provider Plugin source.\\n165: - Provider implementations must be exposed only through `setup({ services })` + `services.provide(...)`, and the same Service Name must be declared in `provides`.\\n166: - Optional dependency behavior must declare `optionalInject`, call `usePluginService(...)`, and tolerate `undefined` with a complete fallback.\\n167: - `setup({ services }).get(X)` requires X to appear in `inject` or `optionalInject`. A component `usePluginService(X)` may also read a Service declared by its own definition in `provides`; Application-owned lookup remains unrestricted.\\n168: - `provides`, `inject`, and `optionalInject` are pairwise disjoint.\\n169: - When multiple Plugins share a capability, reuse an existing seam name/type from `/services/*` and never invent a synonym service contract.\\n170: - Prefer `UIPluginObservableService` only when other Plugins need sustained observation of service-owned state.\\n171: - `UIPluginObservableService` requires `getSnapshot()` + `subscribe()`; otherwise prefer a structural interface with explicit methods.\\n172: - Structural interface service examples are acceptable, and `EventEmitter`-style ad-hoc emitters should remain project-local, not runtime API additions.\\n173: - Do not place capability implementations into Plugin actions or Agent Runtime actions.\\n174: - A Frontend Tool is an Agent-facing adapter for a selected capability operation; it is not a Plugin capability and is not registered by a Plugin.\\n175: - When the product explicitly asks the Agent to invoke frontend behavior, first reuse an existing stable Service seam, have the Provider Plugin declare `provides`, and expose the selected operation from `/agent-contract/agent-tools.ts`. Implement necessary project Service code with ordinary project tools.\\n176: - Frontend Tool names use `lower_snake_case`, inputs use `z.strictObject(...)`, descriptions explain when to call the Tool plus what it does and does not do, and results stay short, structured, and serializable.\\n177: - Frontend Tool handlers call `services.get(...)` and must tolerate a capability disappearing before execution. Never bind a Tool to a React component, ref, DOM query, Plugin instance, or concrete Provider implementation.\\n178: - Do not automatically expose every Service method. A Service may have zero, one, or many explicitly authorized Frontend Tools.\\n179: - Never generate `context.tools.register(...)`, `services.registerTool(...)`, `plugin.registerTool(...)`, or another Plugin self-registration API. Frontend Tool exposure is an Application permission boundary.\\n180: - Provider implementation lifetime is the Plugin activation lifetime; consumers should always read through runtime services instead of direct imports.\\n181: - Do not couple a generated Plugin to Creator packages or Creator UI dependencies.\\n182: - Do not modify `/runtime` or `/framework` for Plugin-specific behavior.\\n183: - Do not rewrite unrelated registration entries.\\n184: - Hiding, removing an instance, and replacing a feature all preserve Plugin source. Do not delete a Plugin directory with generic file tools. Permanent source deletion may only use the dedicated gated domain tool after exact authorization and reference checks; if that tool is unavailable, report the gate instead of approximating it.\\n185: \\n186: \\n187: ## Frontend Tool capability consumers\\n188: \\n189: A Plugin capability consumed by an application-owned Frontend Tool is a valid\\n190: cross-boundary reason for a public Service seam: Plugin provides Service,\\n191: Frontend Tool consumes Service. Preserve Service ownership and public contracts;\\n192: Service existence does not grant Agent exposure permission.\\n193: \\n194: Plugin Component effects manage UI/component lifecycle only. They must never\\n195: simulate Frontend Tool execution by opening a dialog, navigating or mutating a\\n196: capability when a Tool renderer mounts. Follow the `ag-ui-frontend` skill's\\n197: Frontend Tool execution and replay contract. For integration details, read the\\n198: packaged [Frontend Tool lifecycle reference](../../ag-ui-frontend/references/frontend-tool-lifecycle.md).\\n199: \\n200: \\n201: \\n202: ## Delivery obligations\\n203: \\n204: For new-Plugin gap discovery, `inspect_ui_capabilities({})` returns two current\\n205: Operator results: plugins from list_ui_plugins and services from inspect_ui_services.\\n206: It has no detail or cursor parameters and does not include formal Source Items\\n207: or a project component index. Use inspect_agent_ui_sources separately for formal\\n208: resources and targeted file tools for project components. Do not infer absence\\n209: from this combined Plugin/Service result alone. Filenames never prove component\\n210: behavior. Inspect the selected implementation and reuse it whenever it fits.\\n211: \\n212: Existing project Plugin behavior is edited directly. Ask `prepare_ui_plugin_development` only when creating a new Plugin identity, then implement its necessary supporting files and parent edits. File lists are implementation notes, not permissions. Formal Source Item lookup is needed only for a relevant unknown resource.\\n213: \\n214: Before creating a new Plugin, `prepare_ui_plugin_development` requires only\\n215: `targetPluginId` and a short `desiredOutcome`. Ask whether to develop it; do not\\n216: settle implementation dependencies or test design merely to ask this question.\\n217: Optional `deliveryContract` details may be supplied after confirmation without\\n218: asking again: capability, renderingCategory, placement, lifecycle, dependencies,\\n219: verificationMethod, interactions and optional geometry. They are verification\\n220: inputs, never file permissions.\\n221: \\n222: Creation, registration, enabled composition, static validation, Runtime observation,\\n223: and behavioral validation are separate facts. The Host completion gate derives\\n224: delivery from those facts at the current revision. `static_only` cannot establish\\n225: Runtime or interaction success. Missing placement or verification leaves a blocked\\n226: receipt naming saved changes and the last successful stage.\\n227: \\n228: For declared interactions, the Host tool `verify_ui_plugin_behavior` runs the\\n229: project's installed Playwright configuration. Test titles must exactly match\\n230: `[delivery:<pluginId>] <interaction>`; use `runtime` when the browser-test method has\\n231: no interaction list. Every required test must pass without skips or flaky retries.\\n232: Reuse existing test infrastructure and respect the writable project boundary;\\n233: if tests/configuration cannot be supplied within that boundary, report the blocker.\\n234: Do not replace an absent browser test with a model-written PASS claim. Composer\\n235: adapters require send, stop, attachment add/remove/attachment-only send, and draft\\n236: parity for the capabilities already enabled in the target project.\\n237: \\n238: \\n239: ## Localization ownership\\n240: \\n241: Vendor-owned code must remain locale-agnostic and unmodified; all product\\n242: localization is owned by Ag\",\"offset\":16000,\"nextOffset\":24000,\"totalCharacters\":26123}}","role":"tool"}

